{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The wired earbuds relate to my previous headset purchase, so they fit an interest I have shown, although I have no reason to replace my headset now.",
    "The HDMI cable fits my history of buying practical connection accessories, but I would need a device that requires HDMI before choosing it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Smart speakers and streaming devices do not address the computer connection needs reflected in my recent purchases.",
    "A tablet mount does not mean I need a new tablet or a television wall mount; those purchases serve different purposes.",
    "The Wi-Fi extender and memory card would only interest me if I had a coverage or storage problem, and my history does not establish either need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in specific electronics accessories seems to have been stretched into an interest in household electronics generally.",
    "Buying a mount or networking adapter seems to have been treated as a reason to buy other mounts or networking products, even when they solve different problems."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases tend to solve specific connection or compatibility needs, so the exact connector, device and purpose matter to me.",
    "My interactions are infrequent and spread across years; an old purchase is a weak reason to assume I need a replacement or upgrade now.",
    "My latest purchase was a wired Ethernet adapter, which does not by itself suggest that I need better Wi-Fi coverage."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in practical accessories but stretched it into unrelated electronics purchases without a clear current need."
}"}
